<title>USA: U.S. mortgage refinancing volume up 9.1 pct.</title>
<headline>U.S. mortgage refinancing volume up 9.1 pct.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The volume of U.S. mortgage refinancing applications rose 9.1 percent in the week ended July 18, according to a Mortgage Bankers Association of America weekly survey.</p>
<p>The total volume of mortgage applications gained 1.4 percent in the latest survey week, while applications to purchase mortgages dropped 1.5 percent.</p>
<p>The seasonally adjusted refinancing index rose 9.1 percent to 542.8 from 497.3 percent the previous week. The purchase index dipped 2.1 percent to 208.4 in the latest survey from 212.9 in the previous week.</p>
